  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 experiments all use multiprofile + scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, with transformer+weighted (config_027, 0.7250) as the current best. All four aggregation/fusion combinations within that space have been tested, so further multiprofile variants with the same encoders offer no new information. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the singleprofile architecture (no aggregation step) with the same strong encoders could match or exceed the multiprofile results, perhaps by avoiding aggregation-induced noise. This experiment (config_042) tests singleprofile + scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion, directly extending the best-performing encoder/fusion pair into the untested singleprofile regime. It is the best use of the final experiment because: (1) it uses the proven-best encoders and the slightly superior weighted fusion, (2) it explores the one major architectural axis (profile setting) not yet combined with these top encoders, and (3) it is expected to be relatively cheap (~2–3 GPU hours) since it omits the multiprofile aggregation step, keeping total budget low while giving a genuine shot at beating 0.725."
}

